<p>The British government has released more than 100 pages of internal documents from the 2024 process that led Prime Minister Keir Starmer to appoint senior Labour figure Peter Mandelson as the U.K.’s ambassador to Washington. The papers show officials warned of “reputational risks” tied to Mandelson’s past association with convicted sex offender Jeffrey Epstein. Starmer later removed Mandelson from the post in September, after further reporting clarified the “depth and extent” of the relationship, according to the coverage.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/slzwj5kkH6hwv7iYQ4q3YVBGnHafjf0XdqlmusA8qOFhigoIRCIqfg7nF2-NCW1MCy_cU65qCEUwnRbcOPOTz7ImbV_ClHpa802u2zqdF6oemxviq4vHdU2MaACogQ5oZvGYRxlCI1AtXVZENT4vZIAmXfDW2uDWjnmcyDj4oBn9qLi8Hub_xbYoYXByGqb-RmMTkepKYkuXag' alt='Peter Mandelson and Prime Minister Keir Starmer in Washington, in February last year.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Vetting memo: A key vetting note dated 4 December 2024 warned that Mandelson’s relationship with Epstein continued after Epstein’s 2008 conviction, including across 2009–2011.</li><li>Specific allegation: The documents say Mandelson reportedly stayed at Epstein’s house while Epstein was jailed in June 2009.</li><li>Internal disagreement: Politico says the files show national security adviser Jonathan Powell and a senior Foreign Office official raised concerns, while Starmer’s chief of staff Morgan McSweeney pushed to finalize the appointment.</li><li>Politics vs. process: Politico frames the release as evidence that Downing Street had a formal process, but that the final call was political rather than purely procedural.</li><li>Domestic fallout: Dawn says the publication revived questions about Starmer’s judgement and did little to ease political pressure over the appointment.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UK government/officials (released documents): The published files show officials explicitly flagged “reputational risks” tied to Mandelson’s links to Jeffrey Epstein during the appointment process. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/british-prime-minister-was-warned-of-reputational-risk-in-appointing-mandelson-files-show'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Prime Minister Keir Starmer: After removing Mandelson from the post, Starmer said the “depth and extent” of the Epstein relationship went beyond what he knew when he appointed him. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/new-peter-mandelson-files-keir-starmer-downing-street/'>POLITICO Europe</a>)</li><li>Peter Mandelson: Mandelson issued an “unequivocal” apology for his association with Epstein and apologized “to the women and girls that suffered,” according to Politico. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/new-peter-mandelson-files-keir-starmer-downing-street/'>POLITICO Europe</a>)</li><li>National security adviser Jonathan Powell: Notes summarized in the release describe Powell calling the appointment process “unusual” and “weirdly rushed.”. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1981161/starmer-was-warned-over-mandelsons-epstein-links-says-british-government'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1981161/starmer-was-warned-over-mandelsons-epstein-links-says-british-government'>‘Starmer was warned over Mandelson’s Epstein links,’ says British government</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/11/new-files-show-british-pm-warned-of-reputational-risks-with-mandelson'>New files show British PM warned of ‘reputational risks’ with Mandelson</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-starmer-was-warned-of-reputational-risk-in-appointing-mandelson-due-to/'>Starmer was warned of ‘reputational risk’ in appointing Mandelson due to Epstein links, files show</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/released-uk-files-reveal-concerns-on-mandelsons-appointment-as-us-ambassador/article70732079.ece'>Released U.K. files reveal concerns on Mandelson&#x27;s appointment as U.S. Ambassador</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/11/world/mandelson-files-epstein-uk'>Starmer Was Warned About Risk of Appointing Friend of Epstein As Ambassador</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/new-peter-mandelson-files-keir-starmer-downing-street/'>New Mandelson files lay bare what went wrong in Downing Street</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/uk-government-releases-mandelson-us-appointment-files/a-76307838'>UK government releases Mandelson US appointment files</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/starmer-was-warned-of-reputational-risk-over-mandelsons-ties-to-epstein-documents-reveal-13988529.html'>Starmer was warned of ‘reputational risk’ over Mandelson&#x27;s ties to Epstein, documents reveal</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/british-prime-minister-was-warned-of-reputational-risk-in-appointing-mandelson-files-show'>British prime minister was warned of &#x27;reputational risk&#x27; in appointing Mandelson, files show</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/what-are-key-findings-from-uks-release-of-mandelson-documents'>What are key findings from UK&#x27;s release of Mandelson documents?</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>